        "x1": 0.952112676056338,
        "y1": 0.6804603448275862
      },
      "text": "(1) a pig. A pestle of pork is still in common use. \" Pestels of venison,\" Warner's Antiq. Culin. p. 98. *• Pestell of flesshe,^'amJon,\" Palsgrave. A pestle-pie is a large standing pie which contains a whole gammon, and sometimes a couple of fowls and a neat's tongue, a favorite dish at country fairs, and at Christmas feasts. A constable's staff.",
      "html": null,
